WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:02.043
HITONAMI UNIVERSITY

00:02.127 --> 00:04.337
It means that all Heroes

00:04.421 --> 00:07.257
started off as vigilantes.

00:07.340 --> 00:08.425
But now,

00:08.508 --> 00:11.261
with the Pro Hero System in place…

00:11.344 --> 00:12.971
<i>I admired Heroes,</i>

00:13.054 --> 00:15.390
<i>so I decided to call myself a Hero,</i>

00:15.473 --> 00:18.101
<i>but I'm not making a living off of it.</i>

00:18.685 --> 00:20.645
<i>I still have to support myself.</i>

00:22.605 --> 00:24.441
<i>The time I spend at school, work,</i>

00:24.524 --> 00:26.443
<i>and at home.</i>

00:27.068 --> 00:29.029
<i>All in all, those</i>
<i>are the more important things.</i>

00:49.132 --> 00:50.675
I'm home.

00:50.759 --> 00:53.511
Why do I even say that when I live alone?

00:54.095 --> 00:54.929
Hey.

00:55.722 --> 00:57.015
I made myself at home.

01:00.894 --> 01:01.895
<i>This is my house,</i>

01:01.978 --> 01:04.147
<i>but an old man I've never seen before</i>

01:04.230 --> 01:07.609
<i>is eating lunch, drinking beer,</i>
<i>watching TV,</i>

01:09.694 --> 01:11.905
<i>and relaxing?</i>

02:43.830 --> 02:44.664
VIGILANTE
A CRIME PREVENTION ORGANIZATION

02:44.747 --> 02:46.040
THAT OPERATES OUTSIDE OF LEGAL PROCEDURES.
A VIGILANTE GROUP

02:46.124 --> 02:48.710
ALSO REFERS TO MEMBERS OF VIGILANTE GROUPS
WHO ENCOURAGE VIGILANTISM

02:52.088 --> 02:54.257
-Are you a thief?
-Hold on.

02:54.340 --> 02:56.593
-It's me.
-Oh, Master.

02:57.176 --> 02:59.637
Now you know that I'm not
someone suspicious.

02:59.721 --> 03:01.764
Well, I don't know about that.

03:01.848 --> 03:04.726
You were suspicious to begin with.

03:05.310 --> 03:07.979
How'd you even get in?
The front door was locked.

03:08.062 --> 03:09.188
I got in through the window.

03:10.565 --> 03:12.609
How did you get in…

03:19.198 --> 03:20.491
Excuse me…

03:21.576 --> 03:22.702
Who are you?

03:27.582 --> 03:28.917
Hey, who are you?

03:29.834 --> 03:32.837
-It's me.
-Oh, Pop.

03:33.463 --> 03:34.714
You're usually…

03:34.797 --> 03:37.175
Call me plain, and I'll kill you.

03:38.801 --> 03:41.012
By the way,
both of you will start patrolling

03:41.095 --> 03:42.555
at night, right?

03:42.639 --> 03:45.767
My afternoon job ended pretty early,
so I'm taking

03:45.850 --> 03:47.185
a break until nighttime.

03:47.268 --> 03:50.271
<i>He actually has a job?</i>

03:50.355 --> 03:52.649
I have a live performance scheduled today.

03:52.732 --> 03:54.901
I'm going to change, so don't peek.

03:55.652 --> 03:56.486
Yeah,

03:56.569 --> 03:58.571
I won't peek,

03:59.072 --> 04:00.990
but when did you put up this curtain?

04:01.532 --> 04:03.493
What's with this nasty coat?

04:03.576 --> 04:05.620
Stop putting your stuff over here!

04:05.703 --> 04:08.331
Everything on this side of the curtain
is my territory!

04:08.414 --> 04:11.709
What are you saying?
This room is a communal space.

04:11.793 --> 04:14.128
This is my house, you know!

04:16.047 --> 04:19.008
Um… I'm going to work now.

04:19.092 --> 04:22.011
-Go ahead.
-I don't mind.

04:22.929 --> 04:25.974
This is my house, you know.

04:28.935 --> 04:31.437
<i>If you eat this snack</i>

04:31.521 --> 04:33.815
<i>you can become a Hero too!</i>

04:34.524 --> 04:36.776
Why am I here?

04:37.944 --> 04:40.947
<i>I was expecting</i>
<i>something like this, or this,</i>

04:41.572 --> 04:44.450
<i>when I imagined my life on campus.</i>

04:45.660 --> 04:48.913
I haven't made a single friend
since I got into this university.

04:48.997 --> 04:51.124
Stop mumbling and get to work!

04:51.207 --> 04:52.041
Yes, sir!

04:52.125 --> 04:55.003
<i>Your eyes</i>

04:55.086 --> 04:58.673
<i>Are drawing me closer</i>

04:59.299 --> 05:02.802
<i>Can I run away?</i>

05:02.885 --> 05:05.179
Pop-tan!

05:05.263 --> 05:07.932
Hey, is everyone having fun?

05:08.016 --> 05:11.227
<i>This is</i>

05:11.311 --> 05:14.397
<i>Love</i>

05:14.480 --> 05:18.818
<i>I realized for the first time</i>

05:19.485 --> 05:25.283
<i>When I look up</i>
<i>And see you soaring across the sky</i>

05:26.993 --> 05:31.664
<i>My heart skips a beat</i>

05:31.748 --> 05:34.834
<i>Don't let it stop</i>

05:38.046 --> 05:40.423
Ready for the next song?

05:40.506 --> 05:42.258
Yeah!

05:42.341 --> 05:44.594
Get in line if you want to shake my hand!

05:44.677 --> 05:47.972
-Yeah!
-Pop-tan!

05:51.893 --> 05:54.729
<i>With a pop heart</i>

05:54.812 --> 05:57.023
<i>And a pop beat</i>

05:57.690 --> 06:00.777
<i>Sending my love to you</i>

06:00.860 --> 06:03.696
<i>Pop with Hip the Hop</i>

06:07.283 --> 06:09.160
I want to shake her hand too.

06:09.869 --> 06:12.622
<i>That smile you showed me that day</i>

06:12.705 --> 06:15.625
What the hell? Stop cutting in line!

06:16.459 --> 06:17.585
<i>I've been searching for it</i>

06:18.211 --> 06:20.088
Are you all right?

06:20.963 --> 06:23.716
I know you want to get close,
but cutting is dangerous.

06:23.800 --> 06:26.844
-You shouldn't do it.
-That's right.

06:26.928 --> 06:29.972
She's cute, so it's only natural

06:30.056 --> 06:33.643
that you'd want to get one step closer
to touch her.

06:33.726 --> 06:35.103
Did he just say cute?

06:35.186 --> 06:38.064
-<i>Shine</i>
-Shine!

06:38.147 --> 06:42.110
-<i>Sparkle</i>
-Sparkle!

06:42.193 --> 06:44.821
<i>P-O-P S-T-E-P</i>

06:44.904 --> 06:47.240
<i>Let it reach you</i>

06:47.323 --> 06:50.368
-<i>And shine</i>
-Shine!

06:50.451 --> 06:52.954
-<i>Sparkle</i>
-Sparkle!

06:53.037 --> 06:56.165
But if everyone pushes forward
with that selfish mentality,

06:56.249 --> 06:58.251
we'll end up making her cry.

06:58.876 --> 07:00.878
This is where you should show restraint

07:00.962 --> 07:03.673
and cheer her on
from where you are right now.

07:03.756 --> 07:05.758
That's what being a real man is about.

07:06.384 --> 07:07.969
Great advice, Partner!

07:08.052 --> 07:09.262
Yup.

07:09.762 --> 07:12.765
I will convert my burning emotions
into light.

07:12.849 --> 07:14.475
For a love explosion!

07:14.559 --> 07:16.144
Meganetic

07:16.227 --> 07:18.479
Blaster!

07:20.106 --> 07:22.191
Pop-tan!

07:22.275 --> 07:23.734
Amazing!

07:23.818 --> 07:26.320
Thanks for your overwhelming support!

07:26.404 --> 07:27.280
Hee hee.

07:27.363 --> 07:30.533
Hee hee? Why are you standing out
all on your own?

07:30.616 --> 07:32.535
What happened to being a real man?

07:35.913 --> 07:39.459
You guys need to shut up.

07:41.002 --> 07:42.628
Did you say something?

07:43.921 --> 07:45.798
I also… I will…

07:50.636 --> 07:51.471
I will

07:52.138 --> 07:55.433
shake Pop-tan's hand!

07:56.225 --> 07:57.435
-Whoa!
-What's wrong with him?

07:58.352 --> 07:59.562
What's this slimy stuff?

07:59.645 --> 08:01.439
Let's shake hands.

08:04.942 --> 08:06.819
I'll be leaving now.

08:08.154 --> 08:10.156
Another tough day at work.

08:12.450 --> 08:14.494
I'll rest a little
until the evening patrol…

08:15.995 --> 08:17.079
Pop?

08:20.041 --> 08:21.626
Pop-tan!

08:22.793 --> 08:24.962
What the hell is going on?

08:25.046 --> 08:26.339
My concert is ruined now.

08:26.422 --> 08:27.548
We need to help Pop-tan.

08:27.632 --> 08:29.425
Pop-tan!

08:29.509 --> 08:31.844
You guys! What's happening?

08:31.928 --> 08:34.055
-The Squalor.
-The Crawler!

08:35.598 --> 08:36.849
I'm here too.

08:38.643 --> 08:39.769
Fist Geezer!

08:40.978 --> 08:42.063
Those movements

08:42.146 --> 08:44.398
will be a hassle to restrain
once he tries to escape us.

08:47.485 --> 08:48.486
The pincer movement.

08:50.655 --> 08:52.615
-I'll meet you up ahead.
-Yes, sir.

08:54.700 --> 08:56.285
Handshake!

09:00.122 --> 09:03.918
How persistent! You're so creepy!

09:05.419 --> 09:07.421
-I got him!
-Koichi!

09:08.589 --> 09:10.967
Perfect, keep him still.

09:18.182 --> 09:19.016
Are you okay?

09:19.809 --> 09:22.270
That slimy substance is troublesome.

09:25.064 --> 09:26.941
UDON

09:27.942 --> 09:29.026
Pop-tan!

09:39.704 --> 09:42.957
Pop-tan? Where are you?

09:43.040 --> 09:44.709
Hey there.

09:44.792 --> 09:46.043
Pop-tan!

09:46.127 --> 09:48.337
We'll make a special exception today

09:48.421 --> 09:51.507
and hold a private handshake event,
with just you and me.

09:52.216 --> 09:53.342
<i>Handshake?</i>

09:53.426 --> 09:55.636
I heard from some other fans

09:55.720 --> 09:58.264
that he wants a handshake.

09:58.347 --> 10:00.975
He might calm down
once he gets what he wants.

10:01.058 --> 10:04.687
While you're at it, let him grab
your butt too. You've got nothing to lose.

10:04.770 --> 10:07.898
That's what I really hate about you,
Old Man.

10:09.942 --> 10:11.360
Handshake!

10:16.157 --> 10:19.994
<i>I'm an idol. I'm an idol.</i>

10:20.077 --> 10:23.164
<i>And this is a very enthusiastic fan…</i>

10:25.082 --> 10:27.335
<i>That's what he is…</i>

10:27.418 --> 10:30.254
-<i>Right?</i>
-Pop-tan.

10:30.338 --> 10:32.173
Then…

10:32.256 --> 10:33.966
can I…

10:34.050 --> 10:37.303
hug you next? Hug!

10:37.386 --> 10:38.929
Stop! Stop!

10:39.013 --> 10:41.807
Let's kiss! Kiss!

10:47.021 --> 10:48.939
What is this?

10:49.523 --> 10:51.400
It's flour from the udon shop.

10:51.484 --> 10:53.027
Koichi!

10:53.736 --> 10:56.364
We'll let the flour absorb
that mucosal fluid,

10:56.447 --> 10:58.866
and once the slimy substance is gone,
we can start cooking.

10:59.909 --> 11:01.369
Got it?

11:06.165 --> 11:08.417
We couldn't get any leads
from this guy either.

11:09.293 --> 11:13.672
Well, Villains who transform using Trigger
are usually naked.

11:13.756 --> 11:15.424
<i>Since their clothes rip apart.</i>

11:16.050 --> 11:18.803
That's why we have to beat them up
before they transform.

11:20.596 --> 11:23.766
The police are coming.
Should we go our own way now?

11:23.849 --> 11:25.643
Hold on a minute.

11:27.269 --> 11:29.563
I need to take a bath.

11:32.817 --> 11:34.235
By the way, Koichi,

11:34.819 --> 11:37.113
you need to buy good quality shampoo.

11:37.196 --> 11:38.697
The kind without silicone.

11:38.781 --> 11:41.075
The cheap stuff will damage my hair.

11:41.742 --> 11:44.120
Hey, Koichi, what's going on here?

11:44.203 --> 11:45.746
We're out of beer.

11:45.830 --> 11:48.040
You drank all of it.

11:48.124 --> 11:50.084
Is that right? Make sure to restock it.

11:52.795 --> 11:56.549
Hey, Old Man! Stop walking around
without your clothes on!

11:57.133 --> 11:59.051
I'm not on your side of the curtain.

11:59.135 --> 12:02.930
I'm talking about showing good manners
in this communal space.

12:03.013 --> 12:05.307
And smoke outside.
The smell will cling to me.

12:05.391 --> 12:06.559
-Um…
-I can't be an idol

12:06.642 --> 12:08.060
that reeks of cigarettes.

12:08.144 --> 12:11.605
You're still a little baby in diapers,
so stop worrying about things like that.

12:11.689 --> 12:12.565
What…

12:12.648 --> 12:15.568
I'll go hang up the laundry.

12:15.651 --> 12:18.154
Are you saying that I smell?
I don't smell!

12:18.237 --> 12:20.990
Plus, let me also add…

12:21.073 --> 12:23.742
<i>I don't think this was the life</i>
<i>I was expecting</i>

12:24.368 --> 12:26.120
<i>as a university student.</i>

12:27.663 --> 12:29.540
This is ridiculous!

12:30.040 --> 12:32.042
Don't nitpick the minor details.

12:32.126 --> 12:35.671
Koichi! Do something with him!

12:35.754 --> 12:36.964
<i>But…</i>

12:38.507 --> 12:39.550
<i>this</i>

12:40.468 --> 12:41.886
<i>isn't so bad either.</i>

12:45.097 --> 12:46.807
Within the last few weeks,

12:46.891 --> 12:49.935
there's been incidents one after another
caused by Instant Villains.

12:50.936 --> 12:53.564
All of the suspects admitted to using

12:53.647 --> 12:55.691
Ideo Trigger, a Quirk inducing substance,

12:55.774 --> 12:58.736
right before they transformed
into Villains.

13:01.906 --> 13:03.407
Trigger, huh?

13:03.491 --> 13:06.160
I believe it's called
a Quirk enhancement drug or something.

13:07.620 --> 13:09.955
Its use is unauthorized in this country.

13:10.039 --> 13:12.541
But that drug is circulating
in the black market right now?

13:13.501 --> 13:16.128
Basically, it's a dreamlike drug
that gives you

13:16.212 --> 13:18.005
a Hero-level Quirk in an instant.

13:18.631 --> 13:20.299
Tanuma-san.

13:20.382 --> 13:21.759
Oh, sorry.

13:21.842 --> 13:25.513
Social order takes precedence
over any dream, of course.

13:25.596 --> 13:27.389
Most of the incidents

13:27.473 --> 13:29.475
have been occurring in very limited areas.

13:30.059 --> 13:31.977
The downtown area near the train stations

13:32.061 --> 13:33.896
and around East Naruhata.

13:34.605 --> 13:36.440
That's a sketchy area.

13:36.524 --> 13:38.984
But since the location has been
narrowed down that much,

13:39.068 --> 13:41.195
you can trace the drugs
back to the source, right?

13:41.278 --> 13:42.154
But

13:42.238 --> 13:45.491
all the suspects who transformed
into Villains say the same thing.

13:45.574 --> 13:48.744
"I received the drug from someone
I've never met before."

13:48.827 --> 13:50.204
What the hell?

13:50.287 --> 13:51.997
They're handing it out for free?

13:52.081 --> 13:54.625
Maybe it's samples of a new drug.

13:54.708 --> 13:56.460
Could that be it?

13:56.544 --> 13:58.337
Drugs are expensive.

13:58.420 --> 14:00.464
Would they just scatter them like that?

14:00.548 --> 14:02.383
But what other objective could it be?

14:02.466 --> 14:05.678
That's the big question. The objective.

14:06.303 --> 14:09.431
Tsukauchi, this is just my hunch,

14:09.515 --> 14:11.642
but this might not be
a regular drug dealing.

14:12.268 --> 14:15.479
It could be something to make a political
statement, disturbance of public order,

14:15.563 --> 14:18.232
or perhaps just a large-scale
money-making strategy.

14:18.315 --> 14:22.069
Either way, it's somewhat of
an "investment" towards a bigger purpose.

14:23.612 --> 14:25.614
Oops, I guess I'm letting
my imagination run wild.

14:25.698 --> 14:28.325
I have to keep focused on reality.

14:30.327 --> 14:32.580
You got a message? From who?

14:33.497 --> 14:36.250
You know those two middle schooler
fans of mine?

14:36.333 --> 14:38.127
Oh, yeah those two.

14:38.210 --> 14:40.087
<i>Pop-tan!</i>

14:40.671 --> 14:42.840
What does the message say?

14:42.923 --> 14:44.300
I guess they reunited

14:44.383 --> 14:48.095
<i>with the Villain from the other day,</i>
<i>and they became friends.</i>

14:48.178 --> 14:51.682
The other day? You mean that slimy guy?

14:51.765 --> 14:54.059
-He was released?
-Well,

14:54.143 --> 14:57.897
<i>he was slimy, but I guess</i>
<i>he didn't mean to cause any harm.</i>

14:57.980 --> 15:00.107
<i>Apparently, he was also tricked</i>
<i>into using that drug.</i>

15:00.190 --> 15:01.942
<i>Although he sure caused me trouble.</i>

15:02.026 --> 15:04.653
Anyway, those guys say that he might be
willing to talk to me

15:04.737 --> 15:07.197
about how he got the drug and stuff.

15:08.449 --> 15:10.451
That sounds like an actual lead.

15:10.534 --> 15:12.578
Let's tell Master right away.

15:12.661 --> 15:13.787
Hold on.

15:13.871 --> 15:15.372
That old man will just

15:15.456 --> 15:17.249
beat that kid up again.

15:17.333 --> 15:20.961
<i>Hey! Show me your tongue! You bastard!</i>

15:22.796 --> 15:26.342
Maybe we should go talk to him on our own.

15:26.425 --> 15:27.676
Yeah.

15:30.471 --> 15:32.973
Hey, Koichi.

15:33.057 --> 15:35.059
Don't leave me behind.

15:35.142 --> 15:37.436
You walk too fast.

15:37.519 --> 15:39.605
Are you a slow walker by any chance?

15:40.189 --> 15:43.317
I'm usually leaping
when I'm in these shoes.

15:44.193 --> 15:46.570
I don't want you to trip, so here.

15:55.746 --> 15:58.832
If anyone sees me like this,
it'll become a scandal.

15:58.916 --> 16:01.835
You're not even a real celebrity.

16:01.919 --> 16:03.128
Wow!

16:03.837 --> 16:05.130
Pop Step!

16:05.798 --> 16:07.508
It's really you!

16:07.591 --> 16:10.636
You're so cute.
I can't believe it's really you.

16:10.719 --> 16:12.846
Pop-chan, is there an event
going on today?

16:13.639 --> 16:16.350
You don't have make-up around your eyes
because you're off today.

16:16.433 --> 16:18.185
Your sunglasses are so cute.

16:19.770 --> 16:21.730
Can I get a picture with you?

16:24.942 --> 16:26.944
Thank you!

16:27.027 --> 16:29.238
-All right.
-And who is this?

16:29.905 --> 16:31.448
Is it your boyfriend?

16:31.532 --> 16:34.493
Did we just uncover
your passionate love affair?

16:34.994 --> 16:36.912
That's not exactly it…

16:38.080 --> 16:39.331
Not at all!

16:39.415 --> 16:42.167
Why are you so quick to deny it!

16:42.251 --> 16:44.044
What? Why are you mad?

16:44.712 --> 16:46.463
This person is just my manager.

16:46.547 --> 16:48.590
No, an assistant. No, in fact, a servant.

16:48.674 --> 16:50.426
I see, a servant, huh?

16:51.010 --> 16:54.763
Thanks for the picture. Bye!
I'll be cheering you on!

16:55.264 --> 16:58.392
-You're quite popular.
-Of course I am.

17:01.061 --> 17:03.981
I'm a middle schooler
at Manjijuku Private Academy.

17:04.064 --> 17:05.816
Ichimoku Samazu.

17:05.899 --> 17:08.569
Pop-san, I look forward
to working with you today!

17:09.194 --> 17:11.655
Hey. Nice seeing you again, Squalor.

17:11.739 --> 17:14.533
I'm The Crawler. When will you remember?

17:14.616 --> 17:17.411
Where's the other guy?

17:17.494 --> 17:18.495
Namimaru-kun?

17:18.579 --> 17:20.372
Yes, my partner

17:20.456 --> 17:22.958
went with that guy from the other day
to pick up some fan merch,

17:23.042 --> 17:24.835
and they're heading over here now.

17:25.544 --> 17:28.589
Can we all talk at this cafe?

17:28.672 --> 17:31.300
Sure. But now that I think about it,

17:31.383 --> 17:35.012
it's a little embarrassing to go inside
a cafe in this outfit.

17:35.095 --> 17:36.346
What's up guys?

17:38.390 --> 17:40.809
We wanted to have some tea together.

17:40.893 --> 17:44.354
Then sit here and drink.
Make yourself comfortable.

17:45.522 --> 17:48.859
What are we going to do now?
We got caught by that nuisance.

17:48.942 --> 17:50.152
Oh boy.

17:50.235 --> 17:52.571
Try to get us out of this, Koichi.

17:54.656 --> 17:55.949
I'm so happy.

17:56.450 --> 17:58.327
That really made your day, huh, Hachisuka?

17:58.410 --> 17:59.661
Who's that girl?

18:00.245 --> 18:03.040
I guess she's kind of a celebrity online.

18:03.874 --> 18:08.170
You know that kind of stuff, huh?
You're so strange, Hachisuka.

18:10.172 --> 18:12.591
Did you just see a huge bug flying around?

18:13.258 --> 18:15.761
What? I hate bugs!

18:22.476 --> 18:23.727
I have to head to work.

18:24.645 --> 18:27.356
-Why all of a sudden?
-We're not going karaoke together?

18:27.439 --> 18:29.566
Sorry, I'll pass this time.

18:30.359 --> 18:32.277
She's so weird.

18:35.239 --> 18:37.241
<i>I'm Kuin Hachisuka.</i>

18:38.575 --> 18:40.452
<i>I'm in my second year of high school.</i>

18:42.746 --> 18:45.582
<i>I'm a part-time Villain.</i>

18:47.501 --> 18:49.795
<i>My Quirk is Queen Bee.</i>

18:49.878 --> 18:53.215
<i>My job is to use my worker bees</i>
<i>filled with dangerous drugs</i>

18:53.298 --> 18:56.927
<i>to get this city abuzz with chaos.</i>

19:02.224 --> 19:03.058
-Ow.
-Ouch.

19:16.780 --> 19:20.242
-Villains!
-Come on, let's run!

19:21.285 --> 19:22.494
Hey, Teruo!

19:23.704 --> 19:24.538
Teruo?

19:25.497 --> 19:26.874
Teruo!

19:27.916 --> 19:31.253
Multiple Villain incidents are occurring
simultaneously at Downtown Naruhata.

19:31.336 --> 19:34.131
Request Heroes in the nearby area
to be dispatched immediately.

19:34.214 --> 19:35.841
Yes, sir!

19:35.924 --> 19:38.302
I agree. What?

19:38.927 --> 19:41.889
There's commotion on the other side
of the train tracks.

19:41.972 --> 19:43.557
I wonder if there was an accident.

19:46.935 --> 19:48.645
-Master?
-Oh no!

19:48.729 --> 19:51.148
There are lots of Villains
appearing in the streets.

19:51.231 --> 19:54.693
-Over ten of them.
-What? That's a big problem!

19:56.111 --> 19:59.406
Airjet doesn't disappoint!
He's the first one to arrive!

19:59.489 --> 20:00.699
No, he's not the first.

20:03.452 --> 20:06.371
The first on scene
is Turbo Hero, Ingenium.

20:06.455 --> 20:09.958
Wow! Heroes are arriving
one after another!

20:30.562 --> 20:35.275
Texas Smash!

20:36.485 --> 20:39.738
-All Might is here too!
-They crushed the Villains in seconds!

20:40.322 --> 20:43.200
I guess all the Villains
have been captured already.

20:45.118 --> 20:48.330
By the way, where did Master
go in a panicked frenzy?

20:48.413 --> 20:50.249
Why would I know?

20:52.501 --> 20:53.335
Hey!

20:54.294 --> 20:57.422
Teruo! Where are you?

21:01.468 --> 21:04.596
Kid, there's someone
suspicious around here, right?

21:04.680 --> 21:06.431
A bee tamer!

21:07.057 --> 21:07.933
What?

21:15.315 --> 21:18.026
How dare you hurt my baby bee?

21:18.110 --> 21:19.695
That gets me mad.

21:19.778 --> 21:21.405
Are you all right?

21:21.488 --> 21:24.658
Yeah, I'm all right.
Teruo-kun, you're so sweet.

21:25.242 --> 21:26.493
Okay, let's go.

21:26.576 --> 21:28.578
But my friends…

21:28.662 --> 21:31.456
What? I'm your friend too, right?

21:31.540 --> 21:34.835
-Want to see my picture with Pop-chan?
-Yeah!

21:34.918 --> 21:37.296
<i>Yes, at this moment in time,</i>

21:37.379 --> 21:39.298
<i>we had no idea</i>

21:39.881 --> 21:42.884
<i>who we were fighting against.</i>

21:42.968 --> 21:46.805
<i>The real threat lurking in the shadows</i>
<i>of this city.</i>

21:46.888 --> 21:49.641
<i>The concealed malice</i>
<i>remained unbeknownst to us,</i>

21:49.725 --> 21:51.393
<i>as the transient peace continued on.</i>

21:52.769 --> 21:55.105
<i>At this moment in time,</i>
<i>we were still in the dark.</i>

23:27.155 --> 23:29.741
<i>As Trigger spreads among criminals,</i>

23:29.825 --> 23:32.536
<i>Instant Villains bring chaos to the city.</i>

23:32.619 --> 23:34.871
<i>Facing them will be the Pro Hero Ingenium,</i>
<i>and what…</i>

23:34.955 --> 23:36.123
<i>Me too?</i>

23:36.790 --> 23:38.375
<i>Next episode, "Top Runner".</i>

23:38.458 --> 23:40.418
<i>My Slide and Glide will evolve!</i>

23:40.502 --> 23:41.503
Subtitle translation by: Lili Morita
